  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with PCA and avgpool, which outperforms singleprofile PCA and multiprofile transformer PCA in both accuracy and F1. The main uncertainty is whether PCA is an optimal RNA representation in this promising setting. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, so it cleanly tests whether a learned nonlinear RNA representation improves over PCA. This is a good use of the next experiment because it exploits the current best direction while reducing uncertainty about representation quality before adding more complex multimodal fusion."
}

